## Why veterinary medicine?

From an early age I was fascinated by how living organisms work — precise, delicate and complex systems capable of self-regeneration. Although my parents encouraged me towards human medicine, I always knew I wanted to work with animals. I completed my veterinary studies at the University of Warmia and Mazury in Olsztyn, gaining knowledge in treating all species.

## Experience

Already during my studies I volunteered at the Weterynaryjne Centrum Zdrowia Lew clinic. The biggest challenge — and most important experience — was a two-month Erasmus+ internship at the round-the-clock Vetklinikum animal hospital in Vienna. That experience introduced me to European veterinary standards and taught me to work under pressure in a multidisciplinary team.

## Warsaw and future plans

After graduating at the end of March 2026 I moved to Warsaw and began my professional career at the Vet na Woli clinic, where I'm gathering my first hands-on experience as a vet. I'm developing my skills in small-animal internal medicine and diagnostic imaging. This blog is my way of sharing knowledge — I believe that a well-informed owner means a happier animal.

## My interests

Outside work I love travelling and discovering the diversity of cultures — every trip is a biology lesson in the field. Sport helps me stay balanced and build discipline. In the kitchen I experiment with plant-based cooking, which brings both tasty successes and lessons in humility.
